                                            What Is an API? A Beginner-Friendly Guide to APIs and REST APIs
What is an API
API stands for Application Programming Interface. It is a mechanism that allows two different digital apps to interact with each other.It gives
client a standard way to request and share information safely, without needing to know its internal implementation. 

What is an API in programming?
In programming API acts as a universal abstraction layer that and contract that enables code reuse, modular design, and secure system 
communication.
Without APIs, engineers have to build every single feature, database connector, and operating system tool completely from scratch.

